# outside_the_range_picked_as_ideal
#
# THE DESIRE IS GENERIC AND THE WANTS ARE SPECIFIC, which is the shape the derivation exists for.
#
# A plant is surrounded by samples — its soil, its air — and each sample has properties somebody
# watches. The plant states several ranges for each: what it SURVIVES, what it OPERATES in, what
# it BLOOMS in; one of them is picked as ideal for the period the plant is in. The desire says
# one thing about all of that, universal over every watched property there is: whatever is
# watched reads inside the range picked as ideal for its property.
#
# ASKED BY BAND, AND NO NUMBER IS COMPARED HERE. A reading is the band it is in — below the
# range, inside it, or above it, always those three — so the desire says one thing, that it
# should be INSIDE, and says it once per way of failing. Each block declares which side it is,
# `orexis:violationIs`, so the judgment can say which way. The desire says *it should be
# inside*; the judgment says *but it was below*.
#
# WHICH PART IS BROKEN IS THE POINT, and it is the blocks that say it. A met-test written as one
# pattern — this plant has this sample, which has this property, which is classified thus —
# fails as a whole, and a reader is left with "something about that is wrong". Written as one
# block per way of failing, the row names the way: UNMEASURED where nothing has been read at
# all, BELOW where it has and is under, ABOVE where it is over. The three are not the same
# trouble and not the same repair — a look answers the first and no lever does, water answers
# the second and drowns on the third — which is exactly why they are three.
#
# And the shape tests NONE of the topology. It targets a watched property and asks only about
# that property's readings; whether the plant has samples and which range it picked are what
# SETTLE the band elsewhere, not things this desire could be violated by. A plant with no
# samples has nothing to target and is judged about nothing.
#
# THAT IS WHAT KEEPS A STRUCTURAL REPAIR HONEST rather than what forbids it. A met-test that
# walked the topology would be satisfiable by moving the sample off the plant or by pointing
# `:idealRange` at a range the reading already sits inside — the goal repaired by editing its
# own premises, which is the one repair nobody wants. Asked by band, the only way to meet this
# desire is for a reading to land in its band. Moving the plant somewhere warmer is still
# reachable, and reaches it the way everything else does: the move changes what the air reads,
# and the search finds the move because the closure walks BACK from what the want reads to
# whatever an action or a derivation says will change it. What a world must state for that is
# the connection between where a plant stands and what its samples read — and where a world
# states no such connection, moving the plant changes no reading it holds, and the search is
# right not to offer it.
#
# Which band a reading is in is settled where a reading is written, against the range the plant
# has picked; nothing in a met-test does arithmetic (deliberation is on triples, and a number is
# not special). The bands are stated here as an agent would find them.
#
# The pick is what makes it bite. The fern's soil is BELOW the range picked as ideal and its air
# is ABOVE it — both inside what the fern survives and operates in, both outside what it blooms
# in, and blooming is what is picked for this period. The air's humidity is inside and says
# nothing, so the case shows a silent property beside the two in trouble.
#
# Judging names the watched property that failed and nothing coarser: `orexis:about sh:this`,
# so each row is about the very node in trouble. Two nodes, two rows — and two wants under one
# desire, each about one watched property (derive_wants/).
#
# IN THE PROJECT'S OWN WORDS. A plant is `water:Plant`, a sample is `sosa:Sample` and says whose
# it is with `sosa:isSampleOf`, a watched property is `ssn:Property` of its sample and says which
# property with `ssn:forProperty`, and a reading is a `sosa:Observation` typed with the band it
# is in — `sensing:BelowRegion`, `sensing:InRegion`, `sensing:AboveRegion`. A range states a band
# per property exactly as the greenhouse's world file does. One word is nobody's yet and stays
# this case's: which range is picked as ideal for the period the plant is in.
#
# The clock stands at 2026-01-01T12:00:00Z when the derivation runs.

@prefix : <http://example.org/test#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/orexis/water#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix ssn: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix ssn-system: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/systems/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix pursued: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/pursued/keeper/> .
@prefix ground: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/ground/> .


GRAPH :ontology {
  orexis:WantGraph rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph .
}

GRAPH :world {
  :air_humidity_of_fern a sosa:ObservableProperty .
  :air_humidity_of_fern ssn:forProperty water:AirHumidity .
  :air_humidity_of_fern ssn:isPropertyOf :air_of_fern .
  :air_of_fern a sosa:Sample .
  :air_of_fern sosa:isSampleOf :fern .
  :air_warmth_of_fern a sosa:ObservableProperty .
  :air_warmth_of_fern ssn:forProperty water:AirTemperature .
  :air_warmth_of_fern ssn:isPropertyOf :air_of_fern .
  :fern :hasBloomingRange :fern_blooming .
  :fern :idealRange :fern_blooming .
  :fern a water:Plant .
  :fern ssn-system:hasOperatingRange :fern_operating .
  :fern ssn-system:hasSurvivalRange :fern_survival .
  :fern_blooming a :BloomingRange .
  :fern_blooming ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 24 ; schema:minValue 18 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirTemperature ] .
  :fern_blooming ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 45 ; schema:minValue 30 ; ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture ] .
  :fern_blooming ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 70 ; schema:minValue 40 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirHumidity ] .
  :fern_operating a ssn-system:OperatingRange .
  :fern_operating ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 32 ; schema:minValue 12 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirTemperature ] .
  :fern_operating ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 50 ; schema:minValue 15 ; ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture ] .
  :fern_operating ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 85 ; schema:minValue 25 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirHumidity ] .
  :fern_survival a ssn-system:SurvivalRange .
  :fern_survival ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 40 ; schema:minValue 2 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirTemperature ] .
  :fern_survival ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 60 ; schema:minValue 5 ; ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture ] .
  :fern_survival ssn-system:inCondition [ schema:maxValue 95 ; schema:minValue 10 ; ssn:forProperty water:AirHumidity ] .
  :soil_moisture_of_fern a sosa:ObservableProperty .
  :soil_moisture_of_fern ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture .
  :soil_moisture_of_fern ssn:isPropertyOf :soil_of_fern .
  :soil_of_fern a sosa:Sample .
  :soil_of_fern sosa:isSampleOf :fern .
  :soil_warmth_of_fern a sosa:ObservableProperty .
  :soil_warmth_of_fern ssn:forProperty water:AirTemperature .
  :soil_warmth_of_fern ssn:isPropertyOf :soil_of_fern .
}

GRAPH :desires {
  :inside_the_picked_range a sh:NodeShape .
  :inside_the_picked_range sh:property [ orexis:about sh:this ; orexis:violationIs orexis:Above ; sh:message "a watched property reads above the range picked as ideal for it" ; sh:path [ sh:inversePath sosa:observedProperty ] ; sh:qualifiedMaxCount 0 ; sh:qualifiedValueShape [ sh:class sensing:AboveRegion ] ] .
  :inside_the_picked_range sh:property [ orexis:about sh:this ; orexis:violationIs orexis:Below ; sh:message "a watched property reads below the range picked as ideal for it" ; sh:path [ sh:inversePath sosa:observedProperty ] ; sh:qualifiedMaxCount 0 ; sh:qualifiedValueShape [ sh:class sensing:BelowRegion ] ] .
  :inside_the_picked_range sh:property [ orexis:about sh:this ; orexis:violationIs orexis:Unmeasured ; sh:message "a watched property has never been read" ; sh:path [ sh:inversePath sosa:observedProperty ] ; sh:qualifiedMinCount 1 ; sh:qualifiedValueShape [ sh:or ( [ sh:class sensing:BelowRegion ] [ sh:class sensing:InRegion ] [ sh:class sensing:AboveRegion ] ) ] ] .
  :inside_the_picked_range sh:targetClass sosa:ObservableProperty .
  :keeper orexis:holds :keeper.ideal .
  :keeper.ideal a orexis:Desire .
  :keeper.ideal orexis:metWhen :inside_the_picked_range .
  :keeper.ideal rdfs:label "every watched property of every sample around a plant reads inside the range picked as ideal" .
}

GRAPH :sensed {
  :humidity_reading a sensing:InRegion .
  :humidity_reading a sosa:Observation .
  :humidity_reading sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest :air_of_fern .
  :humidity_reading sosa:hasSimpleResult 55 .
  :humidity_reading sosa:observedProperty :air_humidity_of_fern .
  :soil_reading a sensing:BelowRegion .
  :soil_reading a sosa:Observation .
  :soil_reading sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest :soil_of_fern .
  :soil_reading sosa:hasSimpleResult 22 .
  :soil_reading sosa:observedProperty :soil_moisture_of_fern .
  :warmth_reading a sensing:AboveRegion .
  :warmth_reading a sosa:Observation .
  :warmth_reading sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest :air_of_fern .
  :warmth_reading sosa:hasSimpleResult 26 .
  :warmth_reading sosa:observedProperty :air_warmth_of_fern .
}

#  THE PARTITION a world with a waterer and a heater leaves. It decides nothing here: a result
#  about `sh:this` is about the node that failed, not about a predicate, so no scope holds it
#  and the split is per INSTANCE — which is the finer answer and the one this desire wants.
GRAPH :scopes {
  :dose planning:inScope :keeper.scope.1 .
  :heat planning:inScope :keeper.scope.2 .
  :keeper.scope.1 a planning:Scope .
  :keeper.scope.2 a planning:Scope .
  water:AirTemperature planning:inScope :keeper.scope.2 .
  water:SoilMoisture planning:inScope :keeper.scope.1 .
}

# What each graph IS, and when it holds — said once each, beside the data.
GRAPH :catalogue {
  :catalogue a orexis:CatalogueGraph .
  :catalogue a orexis:Graph .
  :desires a orexis:DesireGraph .
  :desires a orexis:Graph .
  :ontology a orexis:Graph .
  :ontology a orexis:OntologyGraph .
  :ontology a orexis:PublicGraph .
  :scopes a orexis:Graph .
  :scopes a orexis:WorkingGraph .
  :scopes a planning:ScopeGraph .
  :scopes orexis:arrivedBy orexis:Derived .
  :scopes orexis:beliefsOf :keeper .
  :sensed a orexis:BeliefGraph .
  :sensed a orexis:Graph .
  :sensed a orexis:StateGraph .
  :world a orexis:Graph .
  :world a orexis:PublicGraph .
}
